# Screens, layout and touch

## Screen model
- Canonical screens S01-S09 are derived in `src/gui/visualStateMachine.ts` (`deriveCanonicalScreen`). Do not set screen state by hand; add the condition to the derivation and its tests.
- Order of precedence: override, modal (S07), flight (S04), landing hold (S09), voice (S06), touch with open panel (S08), detail (S05), selected (S03), hover (S02), else S01.
- A user journey map lives in the Cursor canvas "Cerebro - screen-by-screen user journey wireframes and front-end map". Update it when you add a screen or touchpoint.

## Layout
- Desktop shows at most 2 panels, touch shows 1. Panels never cover the selected target; use `sceneSafeRect` from the layout engine.
- Voice dock stays bottom-center, `min(440px, calc(100vw - 24px))`. Buttons: Call, Hands, Chat, Nodes.
- Modals sit at z-60, dim the background and pause pointer capture. No new popups during a camera flight.
- Handle the soft keyboard with `src/gui/keyboardInset.ts`.

## Touch
- No hover on touch: the first tap selects. One finger orbits, two fingers pinch to dolly and pan.
- Hit targets are at least 44 px. Do not put essential actions behind hover.
- DOM stays the source of truth for dock and panels; the 3D HUD mirrors it through `hudBridge`.

## States
- Every panel needs empty, loading and error states with real copy. No lorem text.
- Fallbacks (`reduced-graphics-fallback`, `webgl-retry`, `spatial-panels-fallback`) must remain reachable when WebGL fails.
